# .mailmap — f00500 S8a.
#
# Maps every author/email pair that was ever attributed to an LLM (or to a
# placeholder bot / catch-all) onto the canonical maintainer identity. Git
# and GitHub both honour this file for `git log` and the contributor graph
# WITHOUT rewriting history — the SHA-1 hashes stay the same, only the
# displayed author changes.
#
# Format reference: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitmailmap
#   Proper Name <commit@email.xx> <commit@email.xx>
#   Proper Name <commit@email.xx> <alias@email.xx>
# The first form maps a (name, email) tuple to the canonical (name, email).
# The second maps a specific (name, email) alias to the canonical.

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical: Cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com>
# -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Same email, mixed casing of the name
Cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com> cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com>

# Author was "Cartago" but the email was a placeholder / typo / older alias
Cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com> Cartago <cartago@example.com>
Cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com> Cartago <cartago@local>
Cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com> Cartago <cartago@relaxingcup.dev>
Cartago <cartago.relaxingcup@gmail.com> cartago <cartago@local>

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM-attributed authors. Every line here represents a real commit whose
# `git config user.name|email` was set to a model/host. The maintainer
# wrote the code; the LLM supplied the temporary identity.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
